# ] is a clockwise tick and [ a counter-clockwise one, each a tap of 20 ms
# with a 20 ms gap, so 40 ms apart at the fastest. The knob reads the angle
# 4 ms after an input (KnobSettle), once the two axes of a report are both
# in, so every tick is 4 ms after the turn that causes it. The first tick of
# a turn goes at once. The turn of a whole circle from 1000 on queues 12
# ticks, one revolution, which come out 40 ms apart until 1452. Letting go
# of the stick (600) makes none.
